# 2. What today changed, in one paragraph each

**Two adversarial engines, seven passes.** Kimi ran three rounds over the manuscript
prose with tools disabled, then three more aimed at what the first round's repairs had
broken. Codex ran four rounds against the repository — Methods vs code, Results vs
deposited artefacts, Discussion vs implementation, then a re-review of the repairs —
plus a review of the work plan itself. Transcripts are in `docs/2026-09-0*`.

**Twenty-six defects were confirmed and most were fixed.** The list and its evidence
live in `quarantine.md` §6; the per-finding verdicts are in
`docs/2026-09-03-finding-dispositions.md`, which records 43 Codex findings under a
three-state standard (`CONFIRMED` / `REJECTED` / `BLOCKED-ON-MISSING-ARTIFACT`).

**Four of my own confirmations were withdrawn** (§6.6, §6.9, §6.16, §6.27). Three
promoted an absence into an error; the fourth mistook an incomplete read for an
absence. This is the failure mode to guard against, and it is why every disposition
now has to carry a re-runnable check rather than an evidence path.

**The range cost is 1.79x, not 1.34x.** C-1 re-measured the paired runs at the release
build. Every published pair had run at `07ad6fa`, the one commit where `--max-period`
did not bound Tier 3, so the narrow arm ran the long-period search and discarded it.
Sublinearity survives — 1.79x for a 20x widening — but the paper now says why the old
number was lower.

**Filip's six figures arrived and are integrated**, re-rendered with BWTandem as the
only saturated colour. Figure 5 (array self-similarity, triangle + dot plot per
species) is new and not yet referenced by the manuscript.

